 "final_text_tail": "ltiIndex._format_multi`. It turns each level into display strings first, then passes those strings to `sparsify_labels`. `sparsify_labels` blanks any label that equals the one above it. Two different floats that format to the same string, such as `2.015000e+11`, therefore get merged into one group. The fix is to decide which labels repeat by comparing the underlying level codes, not the formatted strings. I didn't run anything or change any file.\n\n```json\n{\"files\": [\"pandas/core/indexes/multi.py\", \"pandas/io/formats/format.py\"], \"functions\": [\"MultiIndex._format_multi\", \"sparsify_labels\"]}\n```",
